    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (81.41) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03), both of whom benefit significantly from facing favorable opposing arms. **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine today; his matchup against Lorenzen is ideal, and his elite sprint speed remains our most vital asset in this 5x5 Roto format. Meanwhile, **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a high-leverage start against Giolito, where the combination of the pitcher\u2019s projected volatility and the hitter's favorable platoon splits pushes him into the upper tier of our daily projections. **Brice Turang** (72.43) and **James Wood** (70.10) also project as strong starts, with **James Wood** specifically capitalizing on the leadoff spot\u2019s opportunity to maximize run production, a decision supported by his strong xwOBA.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Kyle Karros** (46.31), who flirted with our start threshold but ultimately lacked the necessary upside to displace the existing depth. While **Kyle Karros** holds modest appeal, the scarcity of stolen bases meant that our priority leaned toward maximizing high-frequency production, leaving him as the odd man out. We are also monitoring the status of **Jose Caballero**, whose game is a confirmed rainout, keeping him off the board entirely. **Travis Bazzana** (39.66) fell just short of the 40.0 efficiency floor, largely due to a difficult matchup against an elite arm in Wheeler and unfavorable wind conditions. \n\nManagerial caution is advised regarding **Cole Young** (47.85), whose score is suppressed by a combination of the \"Elite Hold\" factor and his position in the lower third of the order. While he remains in the lineup, his efficiency is more marginal compared to the high-output days we expect from **Josh Naylor** (69.73) and **Austin Riley** (65.41). **Austin Riley** faces Irvin, J, and despite a minor historical BvP penalty, his capacity to punish a pitcher with a 4.65 xERA makes him a strong start. We continue to hold **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Carson Williams** on the bench or IL, monitoring their status for future rotation as we hunt for stolen base efficiency.",
